[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628534541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102267#issuecomment-2628534541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102267","id":2628534541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6crEEN","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T22:57:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T22:57:31Z","body":"Most editor icons are designed for a 16×16 grid, so at an editor scale of 75%, they start looking blurry because they aren't designed for a 12×12 grid.\n\nHowever, file thumbnail icons are not 16×16 by default, but 64×64. This means that at 75% editor scale, they're displayed at 48×48 where they should remain reasonably sharp (but not as sharp as 100% editor scale).\n\nI wonder if these icons have mipmaps enabled and the blending between two mips causes this blurriness to occur. This could be alleviated by [using bilinear filtering instead of trilinear filtering for 2D rendering](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7411).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions